usted in one of the country's most expensive Senate contests, with total ad spending topping half a billion dollars. Polls over the past two weeks show Brown ahead by three to five points among likely voters, including surveys from Republican-aligned firms, though a few earlier polls gave Husted a narrow edge. Outside ratings split between tossup and lean Democratic, and prediction markets price Brown's chances near seventy percent.\n\nBrown has raised roughly $68 million to Husted's $20 million, giving him a large advertising edge despite heavy outside spending against him. Husted benefits from incumbency and Ohio's Republican-leaning electorate, but appointed incumbents tend to run weaker than elected ones. The race remains genuinely competitive, with rural turnout and swing voters likely to decide the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7221, "margin": 2.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7246, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6986, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6393, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6851, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7568, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7432, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7463, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7417, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7438, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7437, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6872, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6759, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6875, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.716, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6739, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6435, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6773, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7405, "